          "text": "The user wants to start with just parse_point. I'm in plan mode, so I need to construct a well-formed plan for the unit test of parse_point (C + C++), no edits.\n\nLet me think about what the plan needs to cover:\n\n1. **Files to create**: \n   - C++ unit test: `tests/unit_parse_point.cpp` (or `tests/unit/parse_point_test.cpp`)\n   - C unit test: `tests/unit_parse_point.c`\n   \n   Where exactly? Looking at tests/ structure: `tests/CMakeLists.txt`, `tests/cases.cmake`, `tests/run_case.cpp`, `tests/check.cpp`, `tests/gtest_smoke.cpp`, `tests/input_data/`, `tests/expect/`. So tests live flat in `tests/`.\n\n2. **What they link against**: \n   - C++: `common_cpp_static` (or shared?). Static is cleaner. common_cpp_static contains geometry.cpp + string_utils.cpp.\n   - C: `common_c_static`.\n\n3. **CMake wiring**: \n   - `add_executable(unit_parse_point_cpp unit_parse_point.cpp)` + `target_link_libraries(... common_cpp_static)` + `configure_target(... ON)` (for ASan, since linking ASan-instrumented static lib).\n   - `add_test(NAME unit_parse_point_cpp COMMAND unit_parse_point_cpp)`.\n   - Same for C.\n\n   Wait — a key detail: `configure_target(unit_test ON)` gives `/Zi /fsanitize=address` on MSVC and `-g -fsanitize=address` on GCC/Clang. The unit test exe MUST match the library's sanitizer flags. The libraries common_cpp_static/common_c_static are built with `configure_target(ON)`, so they're ASan-instrumented. So the unit test needs ASan too. Yes, `ON`.\n\n   But wait — there's a subtlety about where to put this in tests/CMakeLists.txt. The `configure_target` function is defined in the root CMakeLists.txt before `add_subdirectory(tests)`, so it's visible. `common_cpp_static` / `common_c_static` targets are defined in `common/CMakeLists.txt` via `add_subdirectory(common)` which happens BEFORE `add_subdirectory(tests)` in root. So they're available. Good.\n\n4. **Test structure** — the naked check harness. I need to describe:\n   - C++: helper `check_