n is fixed (the `clean_n` → `lineN` and the missing brace).\n\nWait, let me verify the brace. Lines 30-33:\n```c\n30:     if (code == NUMBER_EMPTY) {\n31:         fprintf(stderr, \"...\");\n32:         return no_input;\n33:     }\n```\nYes, line 33 has `}`. ✓ Fixed.\n\n**t2_passport_c/main.c:**\n- Line 53: `parse_int32(s_num, &N)` — now `s_num` (fixed from `clean_s_num`). ✓\n- Line 63, 69: `s_num` in fprintf (fixed). ✓\n\nSo t2 C main is fixed.\n\n**t1_dist_matrix_cpp/main.cpp:**\n- Line 16: `if (!std::getline(std::cin, lineN))` — `|| lineN.empty()` removed. ✓\n- Empty detection now via parse_int32 → line 28-31. ✓\n\nSo t1 C++ is fixed.\n\nSo the remaining bugs are ALL in the C parse_int32 (string_utils.c):\n1. `end` declared as `char` not `char*` (line 84) — compile error.\n2. Trailing-whitespace skip broken (line 86): `while(isspace(*end)) --end;` starts at '\\0', so never trims trailing whitespace.\n\nLet me also double-check: is there any other issue in the C parse_int32? Let me look at the full function again:\n\n```c\nint parse_int32(const char* s, int32_t* out) {\n    const char* start = s, end = s + (int)strlen(s);   // BUG: end is char\n    while(isspace((unsigned char)*start) && *start != '\\0') ++start;\n    while(isspace((unsigned char)*end)) --end;           // BUG: starts at '\\0'\n    if (start == end) return NUMBER_EMPTY;               // BUG: comparing char* with char\n    if (*start == '+') {\n        ++start;\n        if (!isdigit((unsigned char)*start))\n            return NUMBER_NOT_NUMBER;\n    }\n    errno = 0;\n    char* end_recogn = NULL;\n    long v = strtol(start, &end_recogn, 10);\n    if (errno == ERANGE || v < INT32_MIN || v > INT32_MAX)\n        return NUMBER_OUT_OF_RANGE;\n    if (end_recogn == start || *end_recogn != '\\0')\n        return NUMBER_NOT_NUMBER;\n    *out = (int32_t)v;\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n\nIssues:\n1. Line 84: `end` is `char`, not `char*`. → `end = s + strlen(s)` assigns pointer to char → error; `*end` and `--end` i